Let  $\omega_1$  denote the nine-point circle of triangle  $ABC$ .  Let  $\omega_2$  denote the circle with diameter  $AO$ ; note that  $A_0$  and  $B_0$  lie on  $\omega_2$ .  Let  $\omega_3$  denote the circle with diameter  $AH$ ; note that  $A_1$  and  $B_1$  lie on  $\omega_3$ .

The radical axis of  $\omega_1$  and  $\omega_2$  is  $A_0 B_0$ .  The radical axis of  $\omega_1$  and  $\omega_3$  is  $A_1 B_1$ .  Hence,  $C' = A_0 B_0 \cap A_1 B_1$  is the radical center of  $\omega_1$ ,  $\omega_2$ , and  $\omega_3$ .

Let  $D$  be the projection of  $C$  onto  $HO$ .  Since  $\angle CDO = \angle CDH = 90^\circ$ ,  $D$  lies on both  $\omega_2$  and  $\omega_3$ .  Hence,  $CD$  is the radical axis of  $\omega_2$  and  $\omega_3$ , which means  $C'$  lies on  $CD$ .  It follows that  $CC'$  and  $HO$  are perpendicular.

