  However, the total number of triangles for \(n = 7\) (it must be a complete graph due to the inequality above) is \(\binom{7}{3} = 35\) which is greater than \(3 \cdot 7 = 21\), thus there will exist \(3\)-cycles, consequently \(n \neq 8\).

