Let  $\omega_A$  be the  $A$ -mixtilinear incircle of  $\triangle ABC$ ,  $T_A$  its tangency point with  $\odot(ABC)$  and  $M_A$  the midpoint of the arc  $\overarc{BAC}$ .

It's well-known that  $T_A, I, M_A$  are collinear. Then,   $$ \begin{aligned}AI\perp IN&\iff N\text{ is the tangency point of }\omega_A\text{ with }AC&\iff T_A=M_B&\iff M_A, I, M_B\text{ are collinear.}\end{aligned} $$   Therefore,   $$ \begin{aligned}AI\perp IN&\iff BI\perp IM&\iff\angle CMI=\angle CIA&\iff AI\text{ is tangent to }\odot(IMC)\text{. }\blacksquare\end{aligned} $$

