The given functions \( f(1) = 24\) and \( f(9) = 2024\) suggests interpreting the coefficients of \( f(x) \) as digits of a number in base \( x \). Let the polynomial be:  $f(x) = a_0 + a_1x + a_2x^2 + \cdots + a_nx^n$ . Therefore,

\begin{align*}
f(1) &= a_0 + a_1 + \cdots + a_n = 24 
f(9) &= a_0 + 9a_1 + 9^2a_2 + \cdots + 9^n a_n = 2024 
f(5) &= a_0 + 5a_1 + 5^2a_2 + \cdots + 5^n a_n = \ ?
\end{align*}

So we check if 2024 as a base-9 number has digit sum 24. We just need to find the exact coefficients for the function \( f(x) \) to be true.
\begin{align*}
2024 \div 9 &= 224 &\text{remainder } 8 
224 \div 9 &= 24 &\text{remainder } 8 
24 \div 9 &= 2 &\text{remainder } 6 
2 \div 9 &= 0 &\text{remainder } 2
\end{align*}
Indeed,  $2+6+8+8=24$ , so the function is \(f(x) = 2x^3 + 6x^2 + 8x + 8\).
