By the Inscribed Angle Theorem,  $\angle DCB = \tfrac12\angle DOB = \tfrac12\angle ADC$ .  Let  $h\coloneqq DC$ .  Then 
\begin{align*}
\frac 9h &= \tan\angle ADC = \tan(2\angle DCB) 
               &= \frac{2\tan\angle DCB}{1-\tan^2\angle DCB}
               &= \frac{2\cdot \frac 4h}{1-(\frac 4h)^2} = \frac{8h}{h^2 - 16}.
\end{align*}
Solving this equation yields  $h = 12$ .  It follows that  $AC = \sqrt{AD^2 + DC^2} = \sqrt{9^2 + 12^2} = 15$ .  Finally, by Power of a Point at point  $A$ ,  $AE\cdot AC = AD\cdot AB$ , whence
\[
AE = \frac{AD\cdot AB}{AC} = \frac{9\cdot 13}{15} = \boxed{\frac{39}5\,\textbf{(B)}}.
\]

