For the numerator,
\begin{align*}
a^3 &= a(a^2) 
= a\left(\frac{5a - 4}{2}\right) 
= \frac{5a^2 - 4a}{2} 
&\Rightarrow \frac{5\left(\tfrac{5a - 4}{2}\right) - 4a}{2} 
= \frac{17a - 20}{4}. \tag{2}
\end{align*}

For the denominator,
\begin{align*}
a^6 + 8 &= (a^2)^3 + 2^3 
= (a^2 + 2)(a^4 - 2a^2 + 4) [6pt]
&\Rightarrow \left(\tfrac{5a-4}{2} + 2\right)\left(\left(\tfrac{5a-4}{2}\right)^2 - (5a-4) + 4\right) [6pt]
&\Rightarrow \tfrac{5a}{2}\left(\tfrac{25a^2 - 40a + 16}{4} - (5a-4) + 4\right) [6pt]
&\Rightarrow \tfrac{5a}{2}\left(\tfrac{25a^2 - 60a + 48}{4}\right) [6pt]
&= \frac{85a - 100}{32}. \tag{3}
\end{align*}

Putting (2) and (3) together,
